# What NOT to send to the Docker daemon as build context.
#
# Two jobs. The first is speed: without this file the context is the whole repo
# INCLUDING frontend/node_modules and .git — hundreds of megabytes copied before
# the build even starts. The second is the one that matters: `COPY` can only
# reach what is in the context, so anything excluded here can never be baked
# into an image that gets handed to a client.

# ── Secrets. The reason this file exists. ───────────────────────────────────
# backend/.env holds JWT_SECRET, the MySQL password, the Google client secret,
# the SMTP app password, MIKROTIK_ENC_KEY and DEVICE_SECRET. An image layer is
# readable by anyone who has the image — `docker history` / `docker save` — so a
# copied .env is a credential handed over with the container, permanently.
# Configuration is passed at RUN time instead (--env-file / compose env).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/secrets.h

# ── Never rebuild from someone else's install ───────────────────────────────
# node_modules is platform-specific; copying a Windows tree into a Linux image
# is how "it worked on my machine" happens. `npm ci` builds it in the image.
**/node_modules

# ── Runtime state, not build input ──────────────────────────────────────────
# These are volumes in the running container. Copying a dev machine's copies in
# would ship stale reports and someone else's backup data to the client.
backend/backups/
backend/reports/
backend/branding/
**/*.log
**/logs/

# ── Not runtime input for either image ──────────────────────────────────────
# Both Dockerfiles build from this same root context, so frontend/ source must
# stay IN (frontend/Dockerfile compiles it). Its build output goes out: stage 1
# runs npm run build itself, and copying a stale local dist/ over it is how you
# deploy last week's dashboard without noticing.
frontend/dist/
agent/
iot/
ops/
dev-snmpsim/

# ── Documentation, history, tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
audits/
docs/
migrations/
*.md
*.mwb
*.sql
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
